Z||000011||mrfixit58||08-24-2001||11:27 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by falconhulk:<BR><B>Ok that means putting a chevy 305 would be the same.  But as everyone knows the 305 is a dog.  Thats why I made the statement I did.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I'll have to agree about the 305 but the attraction to the Caddy motor is it's low weight, high torque, and no expensive transmission adaptors are needed. You get V8 performance and rumble for about the same as a quality rebuild of the tiny 2.8. Like we've all said before, "If money was no object..." <P>------------------<BR>Roy :D<BR>87 GT   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG"> ||||reg||1
